WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.710
Speaker 1: Sometimes we jokingly use the term
brain worms.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:12.170
And what we mean sometimes by brain worms
is somebody's abilities to think critically

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.400
and consistently.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.440
Are either suspended deliberately or just
not functioning.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:21.789
We finally got a very interesting interview.

00:00:21.789 --> 00:00:29.990
Fox interviewed a supporter of Georgia Republican
Senate candidate Herschel Walker, and they

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:37.370
actually asked her, what about the fact that
he paid for an abortion for a woman?

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:42.090
He urged to get the abortion after he impregnated
her.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.090
What about that?

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:48.829
Because this woman is presumably pro-life,
anti-choice, anti-abortion, and he claims

00:00:48.829 --> 00:00:51.410
to be as well.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:55.820
And she says, we've all done things when we
were young.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:59.160
Herschel Walker was a nearly 50 year old man
when this happened.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.140
When we were young, he's 60 now.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.800
He was almost 50 when he did this.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.920
What the hell are you talking about?

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:13.330
And this is an example of the total cognitive
dissonance that exists and the inability to

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:17.280
reach certain people, which is where I'm going
to focus in here.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.820
But let's take a look at this clip.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:19.820
Okay.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:22.829
Speaker 4: The matter to you if it's true
or not and even if.

00:01:22.829 --> 00:01:25.670
As long as he is had a change of heart.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:30.940
I mean, we all do things when we're young
and naive.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.100
He's an adult now.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.710
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:38.930
He was an adult of nearly 50 years of age.

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:41.390
When he impregnated a woman.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.469
Urged her to get an abortion paid for the
abortion.

00:01:44.469 --> 00:01:51.229
And now in this second case that we now know
of, implicitly and menacingly threatened the

00:01:51.229 --> 00:01:56.549
woman he impregnated by saying you would not
be safe if you did not get an abortion and

00:01:56.549 --> 00:02:00.329
the eventual child would not be safe if you
didn't get an abortion.

00:02:00.329 --> 00:02:03.600
So there's a bunch of different stories here.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.049
Let's talk about them.

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:10.750
First is the realization that many of us have
had.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.390
You really can't reason with these voters,
right?

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:19.990
What if that woman who we just saw the interview
with, she straight up says he's changed his

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.860
mind and he did this when he was young.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:23.650
We all do things when we were young, he was
almost 50.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:24.650
Okay.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:25.650
You can't reason with her.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.239
So what do you have to do?

00:02:27.239 --> 00:02:33.310
You have to take the money that you might
spend trying to reach those people.

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:38.180
And instead you have to target rational people.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.319
To just get them out to vote.

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:46.620
So as a political strategy, we've said before,
where do you spend limited resources?

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.260
How do you invest the resources and time that
you have?

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:53.319
Is it on trying to change the minds of people
like that woman?

00:02:53.319 --> 00:02:57.790
Seems quite fruitless, I think you would agree,
at least from an election story interpersonally.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:58.790
Sure.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:02:59.870
Try to talk sense into her.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:04.170
But as far as we have x number of dollars
to spend, do we try to just get out the vote

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.150
from people who already lean in our direction?

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.480
Or do we try to change the minds of people
like that?

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:15.260
You've got to just try to get people to vote
that are already that are not totally bamboozled

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.730
and disconnected from reality like that woman.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.900
That's number one.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:21.860
Number two, this idea of redemption.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:25.910
This is an extraordinary get out of jail free
card for the right, which is important for

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.920
us to understand.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:33.590
Redemption can be used to explain away any
transgression no matter what.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:39.349
As long as the individual has completely,
implausibly repented or said why, they've

00:03:39.349 --> 00:03:40.700
changed their mind.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:45.500
And it's used by the right to never have to
actually consider voting for a Democrat.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:49.510
To never consider that the Democrat may actually
be the better choice, as Raphael Warnock is

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:50.700
in the state of Georgia.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:57.030
We saw this with Trump, Donald Trump, 68 years
of life, pro-choice.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:04.140
All of a sudden, he's running to be the Republican
presidential nominee and he needs some way

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:07.170
to no longer be pro-choice that people will
believe.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.900
Trump comes up with the completely unbelievable
story.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.840
Well, you know, I was very pro-choice my whole
life.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.130
This is Trump story, okay?

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:19.400
I was I used to be pro-choice, but I met a
woman who had a kid and I met the kid and

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.620
it was a great kid.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:24.640
And the woman said, you know, at one point,
I wasn't sure if it was the right thing to

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.310
have this pregnancy to carry this pregnancy
to term.

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.169
I thought about getting an abortion and I
didn't.

00:04:29.169 --> 00:04:30.380
And Trump goes, You know what?

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:35.450
My 68 years of being pro-choice, I flushed
him down the toilet 10 to 15 times because

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:37.710
I met a kid I liked.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.170
That's the story.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.590
I don't believe that that's an absurd story.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:46.460
I know many of you don't believe that story,
but it's a get out of jail free card for the

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:47.960
right wingers who go.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.140
He saw the light eventually.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:53.199
Yes, it took him 68 years, but he eventually
saw the light.

00:04:53.199 --> 00:04:56.949
On religion, we know Trump is not religious.

00:04:56.949 --> 00:04:58.789
We know Trump has no idea about religion.

00:04:58.789 --> 00:05:04.350
He didn't grow up religious or any of it,
but he started saying, I love the Bible.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:06.070
Oh, really, Mr. President.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:07.800
At the time, he wasn't President.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.020
Mr. Trump.

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.850
Sir, what's your favorite passage?

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:11.900
Oh, that's personal.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:13.419
I don't want to get into that.

00:05:13.419 --> 00:05:14.419
Do you believe that?

00:05:14.419 --> 00:05:17.110
Do you believe that Trump is a Bible guy?

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:18.110
Are you a First Amendment?

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.310
First Amendment?

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:22.479
Are you a New Testament or an Old Testament
guy?

00:05:22.479 --> 00:05:23.800
Oh, both.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.110
Oh, okay.

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:26.350
Completely unbelievable.

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:31.080
But the evangelical right eventually came
around and said, well, he came he eventually

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:35.550
figured out the right position on abortion
and he's religious now and he loves the Bible

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:36.550
and blah, blah, blah.

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:41.910
So the redemption story is a blank slate.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:45.060
Get out of jail free card if they want it.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:49.259
If they want to if they want to bury you,
then they don't use the redemption story.

00:05:49.259 --> 00:05:54.639
But as long as you've said I changed my mind,
they completely uncritically accept it if

00:05:54.639 --> 00:05:55.639
it's convenient.

00:05:55.639 --> 00:05:59.100
Now, let's kind of go to the last thing.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.729
Speaking very narrowly.

00:06:00.729 --> 00:06:06.110
And specifically, how do people like this
have a driver's license?

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:07.680
How do people like this hold a job?

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.190
Like the woman who we saw there, she's holding
a kid in the interview.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:13.390
How does she parent a child?

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:19.260
Some of these folks, I genuinely don't know
how they get through the day.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:25.490
I don't know how they accomplish the simplest
tasks grocery shopping, figuring out the right

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:27.370
amount of Tylenol to take.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:30.310
Quite frankly, I don't know how they survive.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:31.310
I don't.

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:34.490
Because they are so.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:37.759
I don't even want to characterize it with
adjectives.

00:06:37.759 --> 00:06:42.910
It's disturbing to think about the number
of folks that are this clueless.

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:46.009
That just live in the country with us.

00:06:46.009 --> 00:06:53.039
And it helps us understand how Trump won and
unfortunately, why Herschel Walker may also

00:06:53.039 --> 00:06:54.660
win on Tuesday.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:07:24.389
If our Georgia friends and neighbors don't
get 

